Source: bitscan-agent
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Bitdeer-Security <kaiquan.koh@bitdeer.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: bitscan-agent
Architecture: amd64
Depends: adduser, jq, python3 (>= 3.10), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Bitscan inventory and compliance agent
 Pull-only agent for the Bitscan manager. It enrols with an enrolment
 token, sends a heartbeat, pulls the jobs addressed to its host over TLS
 and uploads the mandatory host inventory: OS details and the full dpkg
 package list. It has no listening port.
 .
 The package holds three static binaries: bitscan-agent, bitscan-runner,
 which runs compliance checks in a sandbox as an unprivileged user, and
 the bitscan-capread helper, which reads the firewall, audit and AppArmor
 state for the checks and is on by default. The runner returns the output
 of each check redacted on the host. A root user can turn the helper off
 with "systemctl disable --now bitscan-capread.socket".
 .
 It also holds the ClusterMAX scanner role: cmax-helper, which runs the
 one fixed audit "cmax audit -vvv -y" as root when the agent asks over
 /run/clustermax/collect.sock for an admin's ClusterMAX scan, and
 ClusterMAX 0.3.0 (Apache-2.0) under /usr/lib/clustermax. Its socket
 is on after install; a root user can turn it off with
 "systemctl disable --now cmax-helper.socket".
